  "title": "Shape",
  "description": "Immutable local-space collision geometry. A `Shape` carries no transform - a Collider positions it in a body. Having an interior is a capability, not a given: solid shapes expose massProperties, while boundary geometry (a segment, a chain of edges) reports `null` and contributes nothing to the owning body's mass. Read the property rather than assuming an area exists.",
